      en: "The Port of Bahía Blanca is Argentina's premier deep-water maritime complex, located in the south of Buenos Aires Province. It is a vital strategic hub for the export of grain, chemicals, and energy products, boasting a privileged location with a natural draft that allows for the largest transoceanic vessels. The port system includes several specialized terminals, such as Ingeniero White and Galván, which handle vast quantities of wheat, barley, and corn from the Pampas and Patagonia. Bahía Blanca is also a major petrochemical hub, with specialized facilities for liquid fuels and gas. Its modern infrastructure, integrated logistical services, and its role as a key gateway for international trade make it one of the most efficient and important ports in the South Atlantic.",
